        "Comprehensive SCD care: penicillin V twice daily from 2–3 months to at least five years, every vaccine plus pneumococcal and meningococcal extras, folic acid (no iron), net and chemoprophylaxis with prompt treatment of every fever, hydroxyurea, transcranial Doppler, growth monitoring and a written crisis plan — fever 38.5 °C or above means cultures and antibiotics within the hour, and pain means analgesia within 30 minutes with maintenance fluids and incentive spirometry.",
        "The HIV-exposed infant gets nevirapine from birth, DNA PCR at six weeks, cotrimoxazole from six weeks and exclusive breastfeeding with the mother on lifelong ART; a positive child starts dolutegravir-based ART the same day, has weight-band dose adjustments and viral loads, TB screening every visit, gradual disclosure complete by 10–12 years, and absolute confidentiality.",
        "Rheumatic fever follows an untreated streptococcal throat and scars the valves: treat sore throats with 10 days of penicillin, and give benzathine penicillin every 3–4 weeks for at least 10 years after an attack; congenital heart disease presents as heart failure (sweating and tiring with feeds, poor weight gain, big liver) or cyanosis unresponsive to oxygen — small frequent fortified feeds, daily weight, diuretics and referral for echocardiography.",
        "Nephrotic syndrome (2–6 years, periorbital oedema, 4+ protein) is prednisolone, daily weight and dipstick, no added salt and infection vigilance; acute glomerulonephritis (cola urine, oedema, hypertension after a throat or skin infection) is fluid and salt restriction, blood pressure monitoring, furosemide and penicillin with full recovery in most; infant urinary infection hides behind fever without a source and a first infection is investigated by ultrasound.",
        "Type 1 diabetes is insulin for life — injection technique, glucose testing, hypo rules (below 4 mmol/L: sugar, recheck in 15 minutes, snack), sick-day rules (never stop insulin) and the school informed; epilepsy is a daily drug never stopped suddenly, seizure first aid taught to family and school, and the beliefs about possession and contagion answered; long-term steroids need growth, blood pressure and glucose monitoring, no sudden stopping, a steroid card, deferred live vaccines and urgent review after measles or chickenpox exposure.",
